cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Materia: atomic-scale wafer exploration and scanning-probe simulation"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it, and cite the models it used as well. Every result carries the primary references for the model that produced it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Materia contributors"
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rfaisalresearch-lab/materia"
abstract: >-
  Materia is a local desktop application for semiconductor surface science. It
  represents a wafer procedurally, instantiates an explicit atomistic region only
  where the user looks, and simulates scanning tunnelling and atomic force
  microscopy of that region. Structure generation is exact crystallography;
  energetics use empirical interatomic potentials; electronic structure uses
  orthogonal semi-empirical tight binding; and adapters expose installed
  first-principles packages. Every reported quantity carries a provenance record
  naming the model, its approximations, its tolerances and its convergence state,
  and requests outside a model's domain are refused rather than approximated.
keywords:
  - scanning tunnelling microscopy
  - atomic force microscopy
  - semiconductor
  - tight binding
  - crystallography
  - surface science
